{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage","id":1381110,"title":"First Mage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-13T15:02:36-07:00","id":1381110,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> First Mage","content":"Hello forum! Tomorrow will be session 0 of my first ever Mage: The Awakening game! I've been wanting to play any of the Chronicles of Darkness games for years, so I'm thrilled to finally have the opportunity. I'm hoping for some assistance in building my first character! I have a few ideas I'm interested in trying out.<br /> <br /> When I was first invited to join this game, I was under the false impression we would be playing Ascension and immediately fell in love with the Akashayana. I was disappointed to say the least when my misunderstanding was corrected, but perhaps I could still make this a reality. In the character creation section there is a sidebar about Nameless Orders, so maybe I could have my Mage be a member of a small cell of Akashayana that have faded into obscurity (intentionally?) while the new Orders rose. Are Ascension and Awakening unified or separate? Worst case scenario the Adamantine Arrow seems like the next best thing, but it's a lot more broad in scope and much more militant in philosophy.<br /> <br /> The concept of the character is to be a new Mage struggling with personal demons who finds peace and purpose through martial discipline. He would be a martial arts instructor by day and a guardian of his cabal and sanctum by night. To serve this end, I really like the Sphere of Forces, particularly the defensive capabilities. I would think his primary spell would be Velocity Control to slow bullets. I want him to be able to walk into a room and feel perfectly secure from physical threats, and be a threat himself. Supplementary Spheres would be Life for healing and physical enhancement, and perhaps Prime for protecting against magical effects. This makes it seem like Obrimos would be the perfect Path, right?<br /> <br /> When it comes to Paths, I really like the attitudes and experiences of the Mastigos. I especially like the Stygian odyssey* of facing one's fears and moral failings to purge the soul (I'm an edgelord, I know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />). That said, I don't especially like one of the Spheres they are tied to. Mind is excellent, and leans into the moral introspection angle of the Path when grappling with the ethical implications of its use. Space, on the other hand, I don't enjoy so much. I get why it works, sympathy and all that, I just don't find its abilities as compelling or well suited to the character.<br /> <br /> \u200b* &quot;A mage who walks the Path of Scourging through the nightmarish labyrinth of the realm of Pandemonium, at the center of which is the Watchtower of the Iron Gauntlet. Pandemonium is also called the Realm of Nightmares, for its echoes appear to Sleepers most often in their most terrible and dreaded dreams, where they fall from endless heights, never to hit the ground, or run for what seems like hours but never make any ground. Their worst fears or repressed emotions are brought forth in places touched by Pandemonium, to be examined and judged by strangers, who mock and condemn them. Through such a gauntlet of humiliation and submission, a soul is scourged of its sins and is thus purified to reunite, cleansed and free, with the divine.&quot;<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I find the attitudes of the Obrimos to be even worse. Being a shining beacon of moral authority is sort of the opposite of what I'm looking for. Then again, I could do something interesting here. Instead of having the typical exalted experience through the Aether**, his journey was excruciating. Every step was like walking on burning coals, the wind scourged him like barbed whips, and by the end he was barely conscious when he carved his name into the Watchtower wall. Get all the edginess of the Mastigos with the bombastic Spheres of the Obrimos. It's a bit of a stretch though, and I would frankly prefer him just be a Mastigos with a different Sphere specialization. I'm not sure how strict you're expected to adhere to the lore in that regard.<br /> <br /> ** &quot;A mage who walks the Path of the Mighty, gliding on celestial winds through the realm of the Aether and the firmament of the stars to reach the Watchtower of the Golden Key. Only the elect can enter here, guarded by the Hosts with their swords of fire. Lightning strikes any who fly with false wings, like Icarus downed by his hubris. He who would wield the Flame Supernal must not flinch in the face of adversity, and cleave to one of the many visions of the divine.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, current rough draft for this character is: Hector, Mastigos Mage of a Nameless Order (Akashayana). He runs a martial arts gym that is itself a Sanctum that he has been assigned guardianship over by his mentor. He trains to master his physical and magical abilities to protect himself and the world from the horrors of the Chronicles of Darkness, and keeps a close eye on his students for potential Awakenings. He is primarily a Forces Mage, supplemented by Mind to seek diplomatic solutions and Life to heal up after negotiations fail.<br /> <br /> My other character is much less difficult to work. Loosely based on a classmate of mine, this character would be named Apollo, an Obrimos Mage of the Free Council. He's a street performer, a fire spinner/breather with a troupe of Sleeper/walker apprentices and a regular fanbase that he is slowly attempting to Awaken through subtle use of Forces and Prime to enhance his performance. The real life person I'm basing this on is a physical masterpiece, dude is unbelievably shredded, so I'm giving him Life as well to reflect his good health. This concept is pretty much ready to go, but I'm still playing with the prior one. Any tips or suggestions would be much appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T16:27:01-07:00","id":1381130,"title":"","content":"Glad to hear you are psyched. Ascension and Awakening are very different games, both are pretty awesome for different reasons.<br /> <br /> Magic in Ascension is the result of consensual reality and you focus on exploring, defining and spreading your version of it as you grow. <br /> <br /> In Awakening there is one Supernal Truth, but its a weird, multi layered and complex. Mages have been outside Plato's Cave for the merest hint of a moment. They became able to call upon and manipulate the Forms to alter reality. They expand their power by witnessing first hand the supernatural, exploring it and internalizing their insights.<br /> <br /> Philosophically speaking, you could replicate the Akashayana with a Perfected Adept:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Perfected_Adept\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Perfected_Adept</a><br /> <br /> You can find a 2ed conversion here:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e/page24\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...d-to-2e/page24</a><br /> <br /> The focus on action, honor and self improvement is at the core of the Adamantine Arrow. The return to simplicity, mindfulness and martial arts is a focus of the Legacy.<br /> <br /> However, they focus on Forces and Life. But the Astral is open to all mages, so the insights of the mind would still be available.<br /> <br /> Regarding Apollo, have you considered making him a member of the Pygmalian Society ? He seems to be working with a similar train of thought:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pygmalian\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Pygmalian</a><br /> <br /> You can find a 2ed conversion on the first page of the same thread as the Adepts.<br /> <br /> Welcome to Mage:The Awakening, hope you have a blast !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-13-2020, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:49:19-07:00","id":1381171,"title":"","content":"Ascension and Awakening are different games with different histories and metaphysics. &quot;Spheres&quot; are an Ascension thing; the term in Awakening is Arcana. Also, you seem to be mixing editions, given that Velocity Control is a 2e spell and you're referencing the 1e Path writeups as the basis of your pursuits beyond &quot;what Arcana do I want to mess with?&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/pathfinding/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;The lore&quot; with regards to the Paths is essentially that each one starts from a different basic perspective of What Magic Is and how different important bits filter into their view of the Arcana.</a><br /> <br /> The Obrimos are primed* to examine magic through the lens of Power and Command, and look at the thing itself as a complex system \u2014 moral authority is orthogonal to the Path of the Mighty's yen for defining, structuring, and otherwise struggling with the fact that their Awakening relies on a certain amount of divine inspiration (read: leaps of logic that you will not be able to explain to people in language). They deal with the magic of Forms, and the danger of their focal pillar of the soul is handled as a &quot;moral authority&quot; thing pretty much entirely for the reasons that their symbolic correspondences in the Tarot include Strength: power bound by discipline and insight. They're a little less clear-cut than some of the other Paths as far as What Their Magic's For, but if I had to try and put a word to it, &quot;self-expression&quot; would be the one.<br /> <br /> The Mastigos, by contrast, are all about self-mastery; they wrestle their inner demons through the lens of Transgression and Confrontation to force them to work for them, and managing the collection of passions and internal conflicts in themselves and other conscious beings is a reflective process. Perception, placement, and personality make up the core of their fifth of the soul, and the ongoing process of dealing with the Devil is more about identifying and managing urges than putting a name on your dirty laundry. There's a kind of a Ring of Gyges thing with the Path of Scourging, in that Mind and Space are really easy Arcana to exploit but they're also really useful in general \u2014 &quot;diplomacy&quot; is not the first thing that comes to mind as the use for power over The Mind Itself absent the rather restrained exercise of &quot;make myself into a different person who can handle this discussion well.&quot;<br /> <br /> Running through the other three in briefer terms since they aren't the main dichotomy you're going over: Acanthus pursue self-determination, Moros pursue self-perfection, and the Thyrsus (the other less-clear one along with the Obrimos) angle for self-transcendence. They look at magic through lenses of choice-and-consquence, permanence-and-transition, and boundaries-and-intercession, respectively, and the stereotypical view of them, at least, is not quite so high-strung as the Obrimos and the Mastigos, as you could probably gather from 1e giving them a free dot in Composure instead of Resolve. The Acanthus trend a smidgen manipulative, the Moros tend to be pretty chill about things that most people are culturally taught to keep their distance from, and the Thyrsus tend to take the social approach to other worlds even when they aren't the Shadow.<br /> <br /> I'd recommend against having the gym be the Sanctum unless it's specifically for mages and Sleepwalkers or you're having him work a lot of subtle magic there; your Sanctum is a ritual space for you to practice magic in relative privacy, as an extension of the mundane uses of a Safe Place. Is the Sanctum in a hidden portion of the gym? (Could give you something to do with the affinity for Space, at least, if you want to stick with Mastigos.)<br /> <br /> If the magical abilities are the main points of priority for the choice of Path it may be worth prioritizing one angle over the rest and taking rotes and Praxes in the other Arcana \u2014 the free improvisation in two Arcana is the biggest mechanical impact your Path has, but if you're after an Arcanum for just one or two primary tricks then you can take the time to get good at those specific things without needing the whole tenth of All Awakened Magic to come naturally to you.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*hah</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:08:36-07:00","id":1381213,"title":"","content":"If you're doing 2e, I'd recommend against pursuing specific Arcana for &quot;defensive capabilities&quot;. In Awakening 2e, there are things called Arcanum Attainments and you get Mage Armor at 2 dots in any Arcanum. This is basically because any Arcanum is useful for basic things like hurting people and preventing you from getting hurt; they just differ in how they do it. Arcanum Attainments are discussed starting on p192 of the corebook. If you want to defend against bullets, for instance, you could use Fate to just be conveniently lucky that you happened to move in a pattern that dodged them all (think how Domino was portrayed in Deadpool 2). Or use Matter to thicken the air or transmute them into harmless vapors. Or use Death to &quot;kill&quot; their impact. That's basically narrative flavor. Make sure you have 2 dots in something other than Prime or Spirit and you'll be fine.<br /> <br /> With &quot;being a threat himself&quot;, virtually every starting Mage is that: with three dots in any Arcanum, you can cause direct damage with magic. You can also get Very Creative, but you'll have to read up on Creative Thaumaturgy and talk with your ST on anything you try. There's literally too much to cover. There was a recent thread on how to use Prime for assassination, for instance.<br /> <br /> If you're really bothered by the Mastigos write-up, I'd suggest reading through this thread:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1357926-making-the-mastigos-more-palatable\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...more-palatable</a> I'm sure people would be up to doing a Why The Obrimos Aren't So Bad thread, too, if what Satchel said doesn't satisfy you.<br /> <br /> I've sort of... dropped 1e from my brain, so don't have anything useful to suggest there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T22:35:12-07:00","id":1381222,"title":"","content":"Akashic Brothers as a small order should work, but you probably would enjoy the character concept just as well as an Adamantine Arrow or Free Council mage.<br /> <br /> AA are martial, but they aren't all bully boys or bruisers. Their philosophy is one of personal betterment and service. <br /> The Free Council, unlike most mages, believe that Sleepers have valuable insights into the great mysteries, and study their developments for new truths. This means that they would fully support learning from Sleeper masters of an art as a reasonable means of improving one's own Gnosis.<br /> <br /> (Either or both would likely attend classes is your character has the skills to make that reasonable, regardless of affiliation.)<br /> <br /> The Perfected Adepts were created with them in mind. (Pretty sure their 1e write-up even called them Akashi somewhere) That said, if you go with a focus on self-perfection and combat focus, you could be from a number of legacies. (e.g. The Uncrowned Kings are literally attempting to set up their own alchemical crucible to purify their mind, body, and soul.)<br /> <br /> There's a bit of a dearth of martial arts as legacies, so a custom legacy may be more appealing. That's more work but it can be fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> Go take a peek at the section &quot;attainments&quot; after the spells listing. Look up Space. That's great fun for a martial artist of any soft style, at least.<br /> <br /> Outward and Inward Eye lets you see everything around you, granting amazing spatial awareness.<br /> Ground Eater let's you run really fast, which is always nice to have in your back pocket.<br /> Break Boundary allows you to bypass locks and chains. Also nice to have.Fits a legendary ninja.<br /> The martial uses of Ban and CoLocation are innumerable and not all obvious.<br /> Perfect Sympathy fits a martial character who learns about a foe and uses that insight to defeat them.<br /> Alter Direction allows for all sorts of silly wuxia stunts. It's great armor, too.<br /> <br /> So, my suggestions would be:<br /> Don't write off the Space arcanum. Knowing where to strike is an important part of martial skill. Not being where an attack is going to be is another. <br /> Make sure your gym has a locked office or private practice room. That would be an appropriate ritual space.<br /> Consider membership in Adamantine Arrow or Free Council..If not, chat with your ST and see about representing your group with the Cult Merit. While at it, you might consider Martial Arts as a Professional Skill Merit, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T17:02:55-07:00","id":1381473,"title":"","content":"Thanks everyone for your comments! I appreciate the assistance greatly. As you noticed my inexperience with the system led me to conflate 3 different versions of Mage, which I suppose means I'm something of a Space Mage myself. *insert Willem Dafoe meme here* Now that I have the editions straight, I think I have a good idea of what I want to do.<br /> <br /> @KaiserAfini: Thanks for clearing up the metaphysics. I personally like the subjectivity of Ascension better, but I love a good Plato's Cave Allegory as much as the next nihilist. Here's a cool take on it: <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xj7O8mrO_wY\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=xj7O8mrO_wY</a><br /> <br /> @Satchel: Thanks for helping me understand the Paths a bit better. You make an excellent point about the Sanctum and how I could apply Space Arcana to solve the issue.<br /> <br /> @Errol216: Good point about Mage Armor. I hadn't reached that part of the book yet. Also, I actually very much like the Mastigos write up, but thanks for the link anyway. It's interesting to see other peoples' perspectives on the Paths. Another couple videos from Dead Sound tap into the notion of finding strength in one's trauma; &quot;Merry Madness&quot; and &quot;Scary and Strange&quot; which should be watched in order for full effect.<br /> <br /> @thenate: You did a great job selling Space Arcana and the Adamantine Arrow. I need to be more open minded about how magic works. I'm a D&amp;D veteran, so I'm used to stricter rules.<br /> <br /> I like the Perfected Adept, but I don't think I'll be going with it. As was mentioned, they're pretty heavily invested in Life and my interest in that Arcana was for purely meta-game reasons, and seems to require a substantial investment of 4-5 dots to get what I want out of it. I think the new build for Hector will be Mind, Space and Forces Arcana. Gets me access to the core spells I really like, and forces me to be a bit more creative about how a martial artist might use seemingly indirect magic to potent effect. A protector needs to not only be able to endure hardship, but to see threats coming and be present to face them. I especially like the intimidation factor of Ground-Eater. I'm still debating how to allocate dots though. I like 2/2/2 as it gives me solid options with each Arcana and access to Kinetic Blow to sell the magic martial artist feel, but if I really wanted Turn Momentum and Velocity Control would it be weird for a Mastigos to go Forces 3/Mind 2/Space 1?<br /> <br /> He will be an Adamantine Arrow but as a Mastigos not as committed to following the strict dogma and authority of the Order. His gym would have a back office that either is concealed through Mind and Space Arcana or a Demesne. I'll talk to my ST about how best to make it fit.<br /> <br /> As for Apollo, I like the philosophy of the Pygmalian Society but feel very certain he is an Obrimos. If the Society is open to non-Acanthus, then I like it!<br /> <br /> Session 0 starts in an hour, so I'll talk it over with the team and use whichever character meshes best with the rest of the Cabal. Thanks again for the feedback! I'll return with details after.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","user":"ZenBear","date":". 04-14-2020, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T21:52:15-07:00","id":1381525,"title":"","content":"Legacies require either the parent Path or Order. Barring that, if you have good plot justification, your GM would probably approve it.<br /> <br /> The Pygmalians are found in all orders. Granted than in lesser number on the Guardians and Arrow, but still possible.<br /> <br /> Legacies tend to create their optional Attainments from a Ruling Arcanum of the parent Path. So Apollo would have to invest in a Common Arcanum.<br /> <br /> A Forces based Mastigos Legacy is a bit tougher. I can't recall one that specifically focuses on martial arts, the closest thing is the Brotherhood of the Demon Wind:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Brotherhood_of_the_Demon_Wind\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Br...the_Demon_Wind</a><br /> <br /> Perhaps the Illuminated Path:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Illumined_Path\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Illumined_Path</a><br /> <br /> They have a focus on mentoring, plus Attainments to guide and protect.<br /> <br /> Not many more come to mind. This made me notice how rare Forces Legacies are for Mastigos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T23:18:49-07:00","id":1381539,"title":"","content":"Regarding legacies: It's best to pick mostly based on the theme/flavor, legacy yantras, and legacy oblations. In my experience it's very hard to find a legacy that both makes sense for a character AND grants a useful third ruling arcanum unless you design your own, and legacy attainments tend to have niche usefulness because of limited reach and spell factors. Also unless a chronicle is going to run for a very a long time, you're unlikely to reach the gnosis requirements for the fourth or fifth attainments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13121-galivet","name":"galivet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13121_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T09:22:47-07:00","id":1381664,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Since this is the first game, I recommend holding up on making a custom Legacy for now. Right now there is already a ton of information to unpack.<br /> <br /> One more Legacy came to mind, the Exploratores Felicem Spiritum:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1348014-2e-legacy-exploratores-felicem-spiritum-an-acanthus-forces-fate-legacy\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...es-fate-legacy</a><br /> <br /> Their parent Order is the Arrow, primary Arcanum is Forces. Their Attainments focus a lot on speed, freedom of movement and dealing with the terrain, all very useful for a martial artist.<br /> <br /> Their use of Fate could be seen as following The Way / Do. Their scouting focus lends itself to protecting others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-15-2020, 01:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T19:45:20-07:00","id":1381847,"title":"","content":"Here's a few links to some pages you might be interested in:<br /> <br /> Some mechanical optimization: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/928257-prioritization-tips-for-character-development\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...er-development</a><br /> <br /> Cabal creation: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1376067-planning-a-chronicle-cabal-creation-process\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...eation-process</a><br /> <br /> Some good advice on learning the game in general: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1357950-learning-curve\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...learning-curve</a><br /> <br /> There are other pages here on the forums that can help as well, but they might take some digging on your part. One thing I would keep in your mind is to keep a stronger focus on who the person is and what makes them tic over what they are capable of. Interesting games are made of interesting people, less so interesting skills. Of course don't be afraid to leave some of the canvas blank so you can explore it after the game has started, but you'll probably want to answer a few questions:<br /> <br /> What is the character's personality?<br /> What is one of the best memories the character has?<br /> What are two habits the character has (probably emphasis on mental tics over good vs bad)?<br /> What personal trauma has the character gone through or experienced? Is it still relevant to who they are today?<br /> What obsession did they have that lead them to awakening? You will probably want to thematically tie this in to the path they awaken to. Some example questions that can help answer that would be:<br /> Acanthus: What duty is caging you to your predictable routine?<br /> Mastigos: What kind of personal passion do you have: obsession, destructive thought pattern, or spiritual wound? Describe it.<br /> Moros: What heavy responsibility is weighing you down, leading you towards an undesirable change?<br /> Obrimos: Where in your life do you have an ordered, hierarchical system? What does that look like?<br /> Thyrsus: Where do you go to be most alive?<br /> <br /> Last question: Has your character experienced something supernatural before they Awakened? If so, what was it and how did it affect them?<br /> <br /> Finally, consider leaning heavily into and on your aspirations and obsessions. These will inform your ST what kinds of things you want in the game.<br /> <br /> Oh, and if your ST forgets or doesn't think about it, you should ask them to do a Lines and Veils thing (from Changeling the Lost, but it's a great idea anyways). It basically goes like this:<br /> &quot;A venerable old safety technique, Lines and Veils allow players to pick and choose what they want to addressin the chronicle. Before the game, the Storyteller prepares two sheets of paper. Label one \u201cLines\u201d and the other \u201cVeils.\u201d Lines are things the chronicle will absolutely not touch on, not even in passing. Veils are things that can happen, but will not be played out, instead addressed with a \u201cfade to black.\u201d The Storyteller asks players what they\u2019d like added to the lists, and notes that the lists can be edited at any time. Veils can be moved to Lines, Lines can be moved to Veils, new Veils or Lines can be added, or Veils or Lines can be taken away (with the consensus of the other players). Veils and Lines cannot be used to cut out antagonists (i.e. \u201cI don\u2019t want the True Fae to be a part of this chronicle at all, not even mentioned in passing\u201d) but can be used to restrict antagonists\u2019 actions that might be uncomfortable for some players (i.e. \u201cI do not want the True Fae in this chronicle to use sexual violence\u201d).&quot;<br /> <br /> It's less important in a game where trauma isn't part of the main focus of the game, but it's still a very valuable thing to include. Just replace True Fae and other references to Changeling the Lost with appropriate things from Mage and other parts of the horror genre that are appropriate.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7825-falcon777","name":"Falcon777","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T21:44:47-07:00","id":1382058,"title":"","content":"Thanks again for the feedback, y'all! Here's the update I promised:<br /> <br /> After one of the other players in my Cabal decided to play an Obrimos, I decided to play Hector. He's 2/2/2 in Mind, Space, and Forces. Athletics and Brawl are 3 with a specialty in Martial Arts (obviously). Drive is 2 with &quot;Aggressive&quot; specialization, as we've decided to set the story in LA anyone who owns a car there learns to drive aggressive. Expression is a 2 with specialty &quot;Teaching&quot; to represent his profession, though perhaps &quot;Teaching&quot; is too narrow to be useful? Perhaps &quot;Interview&quot; to reflect having to interview students or parents of students on the regular? Gnosis is 2, leaving 5 Merits. I took Adamant Hand so I can use martial forms as &quot;a reflexive Order tool Yantra&quot; (2 dots), and it requires Order Status (1). With only 2 dots left, I picked Safe Place and Resources.<br /> <br /> Hector Awakened while being mugged at gunpoint. The mugger was extremely nervous and Hector managed to get the upper hand, knocking the gun away. The mugger attempted to flee, but in a fit of adrenaline fueled rage Hector stopped him and got him in a choke hold. In a panic the mugger pulled a knife to try and fight him off, but was too weak to be effectual. As Hector choked the life from the mugger he was drawn into the mugger's mind and experienced his entire life flashing before his eyes, and in Hector's mind the mugger became the childhood version of himself as he died. Traumatized by the experience, Hector was nearly comatose when the police arrived. He was acquitted of any charges on grounds of self-defense, but he's haunted by guilt and shame because he knows he could have let the man flee. He was barely an adult, and the gun was later discovered to have not even been loaded. Hector's Supernal Journey occurred during his comatose state, reliving that moment as the capstone to a parade of every mistake he made his whole life played over and over until he reached the Iron Gauntlet and gave his name.<br /> <br /> While in the hospital he was recruited by Apollo, my other character who I am instead making Hector's mentor in the Adamantine Arrow. The Guardians had expressed disinterest in him due to his poor reaction to killing, so the Arrow trained him in their ways. Hector threw himself wholeheartedly into their teachings and swiftly earned Apollo's respect, enough to be granted the title of Banner-Warden of his first Cabal as they begin investigating possible Seers of the Throne activity in LA. Hector is his Shadow Name, last name Zeroni because he loves the book Holes. His real name is kept hidden for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> I need help picking 2 Praxes and 3 Rotes. From what I understand having either in Forces, my one Common Arcanum, means I get to cast the spell without expending Mana, so I'm tempted to take everything here to maximize that utility but that's pure meta-game. The only ones that stand out to me though are Kinetic Blow for obvious reasons and Control Gravity for some Windrunner action. I like KB as a Rote, something he was taught by the Arrow. That means I use Brawl (3) as my Yantra which will give me 3 extra dice in spellcasting? Is this redundant with Adamant Hand? Also, what do I do with all the free Reach I get from a Rote? I can extend KB to a weapon, but that seems pointless when my Brawl is higher anyway. I suppose I could extend its duration by a bunch? I also like The Outward and Inward Eye as another Rote, but again I don't know what to do with all the Reach.<br /> <br /> The benefit of a Praxis is essentially a crit bonus, right? So I want this on spells that benefit from critical successes. I honestly have no idea what spells would benefit from this. I also know these are supposed to be very personal spells that are most often used, so I could make the choice based on that. I don't know what spells will actually turn out regularly useful, but my initial thoughts go to Telepathy for group utility, First Impressions for what's on the tin, Scrying for being a creeper, or Psychic Domination for the kink. I'm not seeing anything in Forces that Hector would want to use regularly enough to be Praxis, at least not when he's trying to be incognito around Sleepers.<br /> <br /> Any tips on how best to take advantage of these perks would be greatly appreciated!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T22:25:59-07:00","id":1382064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382058#post1382058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like KB as a Rote, something he was taught by the Arrow. That means I use Brawl (3) as my Yantra which will give me 3 extra dice in spellcasting? Is this redundant with Adamant Hand?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not redundant with Adamant Hand, because Adamant Hand lets you use appropriate combat actions as an Order Tool Yantra. The rote lets you use your dots in the relevant Skill (in this case Brawl) as a Yantra bonus through the mudra (notably, as an Arrow, rotes you've learned from the order that key off of your Athletics add an extra die to their Yantra bonus).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, what do I do with all the free Reach I get from a Rote? I can extend KB to a weapon, but that seems pointless when my Brawl is higher anyway. I suppose I could extend its duration by a bunch? I also like The Outward and Inward Eye as another Rote, but again I don't know what to do with all the Reach. </div> </div> </div>One of the biggest benefits of Master-equivalent Reach on rotes, especially at low Gnosis, is that you can pretty much always safely cast them unless you're <i>far</i> over your spell control safety cap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The benefit of a Praxis is essentially a crit bonus, right? So I want this on spells that benefit from critical successes. I honestly have no idea what spells would benefit from this. </div> </div> </div>The benefit of Praxes is that, as spells you are especially practiced at, they succeed exceptionally more easily, which means they're more likely to gain the benefits of exceptional success (for which see the spellcasting section's roll results).<br /> <br /> Some factor-intensive spells might be said to benefit &quot;more&quot; from exceptional success, since the list of options includes a free step or a free Reach in the primary spell factor or completely ignoring a target's Withstand rating, but <i>every</i> spell benefits from exceptional success, because the rest of the options on that list are &quot;apply a Condition to yourself or the subject that gives Arcane Beats when it's resolved&quot; or &quot;get Mana equal to what you spent on the spell, plus one more point,&quot; and regardless of which option you take from the list you are <i>also</i> getting a point of Willpower out the result.<br /> <br /> Basically, Praxes serve vaguely the same purpose as your Vice; they're a fallback recovery mechanism as much as they are &quot;signature spells&quot; for folks who can't make their own rotes yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T23:24:38-07:00","id":1382069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382064#post1382064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, Praxes serve vaguely the same purpose as your Vice; they're a fallback recovery mechanism as much as they are &quot;signature spells&quot; for folks who can't make their own rotes yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>I talked this over with my ST a little bit today. He suggests I pick rituals so I can increase the casting time to get more dice, thus raising the chance of exceptional success. Adding in what you say here makes me think these should be downtime spells. My thoughts immediately jump to Scrying and Tune In as things he could do to let off steam. If I understand the spell correctly, with Tune In you basically get free cable? Why buy a TV when you can just lay in bed and magically hack your neighbor's? This would require Reach for range so maybe not, but you get the idea. Scrying would be a bit more questionable, like spying on a love interest, but in just that way it's like a Vice. I would also consider Telepathy to fall in the ritual-able category I think.<br /> <br /> Alternately, I could bank on the occasional crit for ignoring a target's Withstand rating and take Psychic Domination. It would come up rarely, but a situation in which I'm casting PD is a situation where exceptional successes would pay off most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T00:08:22-07:00","id":1382074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382069#post1382069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I talked this over with my ST a little bit today. He suggests I pick rituals so I can increase the casting time to get more dice, thus raising the chance of exceptional success.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't really recommend that in good conscience, seeing as that's a time investment of several hours until you're at the upper third of the Gnosis chart and that's kind of the opposite end of Mage's playstyle dichotomy from where Praxes live; Praxes are parts of your magical identity to such a degree that they're a route to joining some Legacies, and if you have the time to roll dice to try and regain Willpower or Mana then you probably have the time to take a nap or perform an oblation instead. Extended ritual casting is more the domain of rotes, which are both more stable and better-equipped to let you push your limits in a controlled environment.<br /> <br /> Praxes thematically work best as things the character Just Does as a mage; synergizing them with your Shadow Name or your Obsessions will go a long way, such that there's ample grounds to look at them as (variably compulsive) self-stimulating behaviors. Does Mental Scan seem germane to Hector's traumatic Awakening circumstances? (From the other end of the scale, how does taking Secret Door as a rote sound for security measures and general utility?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Alternately, I could bank on the occasional crit for ignoring a target's Withstand rating and take Psychic Domination. It would come up rarely, but a situation in which I'm casting PD is a situation where exceptional successes would pay off most. </div> </div> </div>I should here remind you that the exceptional success mechanics apply to all spells regardless of type, so taking a Praxis that you will hardly ever use is not the best investment. It's also kind of the opposite of what a Praxis is to begin with \u2014 if your character has cast Psychic Domination so often that he more frequently gets a lucky stroke of insight from using it, that <i>says something about his magic</i>, which you may or may not want to explore.<br /> <br /> Separately, I'm looking back over the breakdown and I should point out that you start with a dot of Order Status for free; you've got an extra Merit dot open. Any plans to develop the symbolism of Hector Zeroni as a Shadow Name?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T09:40:16-07:00","id":1382190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382074#post1382074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't really recommend that in good conscience, seeing as that's a time investment of several hours until you're at the upper third of the Gnosis chart and that's kind of the opposite end of Mage's playstyle dichotomy from where Praxes live; Praxes are parts of your magical identity to such a degree that they're a route to joining some Legacies, and if you have the time to roll dice to try and regain Willpower or Mana then you probably have the time to take a nap or perform an oblation instead. Extended ritual casting is more the domain of rotes, which are both more stable and better-equipped to let you push your limits in a controlled environment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382074#post1382074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Praxes thematically work best as things the character Just Does as a mage; synergizing them with your Shadow Name or your Obsessions will go a long way, such that there's ample grounds to look at them as (variably compulsive) self-stimulating behaviors. Does Mental Scan seem germane to Hector's traumatic Awakening circumstances? (From the other end of the scale, how does taking Secret Door as a rote sound for security measures and general utility?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Mental Scan is one possibility, though perhaps it would make more sense if he was too traumatized by his Awakening to be comfortable performing that spell regularly. The spell I see him using most is First Impressions as a professional/social aid assuming it can be cast subtly. Secret Door is good if I wanted to have a Sanctum, but after talking it over with my ST I decided against it. Scrying seems like something generally useful while at the same time having that temptation to be abused.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382074#post1382074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should here remind you that the exceptional success mechanics apply to all spells regardless of type, so taking a Praxis that you will hardly ever use is not the best investment. It's also kind of the opposite of what a Praxis is to begin with \u2014 if your character has cast Psychic Domination so often that he more frequently gets a lucky stroke of insight from using it, that <i>says something about his magic</i>, which you may or may not want to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, PD seems like a last resort kind of spell. That may not really fit as a Praxis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382074#post1382074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Separately, I'm looking back over the breakdown and I should point out that you start with a dot of Order Status for free; you've got an extra Merit dot open. Any plans to develop the symbolism of Hector Zeroni as a Shadow Name?</div> </div> </div> </div>My ST pointed that out and suggested that since I'm a Banner-Warden, that level of trust should be a 2 dot investment in Order Status. The symbolism of Hector is its etymological roots, being both a reference to the Trojan warrior Hector denoting heroism, and the later definition of &quot;bully.&quot; He struggles to ride the line of humility and assertiveness in pursuing his goals. This is where PD could fit as a Vice-like option when trying to get his way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","user":"ZenBear","date":". 04-17-2020, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T21:44:01-07:00","id":1382438,"title":"","content":"Alright, final build (probably!)<br /> <br /> Gnosis 2, Forces 2, Mind 2, Space 2<br /> Rotes: Kinetic Blow, Telepathy, Nightvision<br /> Praxes: Ground-Eater, Outward/Inward Eye<br /> <br /> Kinetic Blow I can cast in 2 turns with 7 dice if I use High Speech, giving me 4 reach for quick cast, a full day duration, and both Knock Down and Stun Tilts. If I drop one or both of the Tilts and/or drop the duration to one scene, I can grant this buff to myself and 4 allies in sensory range.<br /> <br /> Telepathy can be cast in 2 turns with 7 dice using High Speech, affecting 5 targets with the ability for all targets capable of sending and receiving messages that lasts for a scene/hour. Alternately I can target 1 subject at Sympathetic Range for 1 Mana.<br /> <br /> Nightvision can be cast in 2 turns, 7 dice, High Speech, affecting 5 targets at sensory range, lasting 1 scene/hour or 1 day, with the protection against sudden extreme stimulus.<br /> <br /> Ground-Eater can be cast in 1 turn with 6 dice on myself at potency 2 for 1 scene/hour, with 3+ exceptional success.<br /> <br /> Outward/Inward Eye can be cast in 2 turns, 7 dice, High Speech, lasting 1 scene/hour or 1 day, 3+ ES. If I combo this with Nightvision, I get perfect perception at sensory range and a solid chance of ES for recharging Mana/Willpower.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty happy with this set up. I'll let the story guide Hector's progression, but he's probably going to bump Forces to 3 and start learning Rotes for Telekinetic Strike, Turn Momentum, and Velocity Control. Bump Gnosis before or after, I'm open to being persuaded of its greater importance.<br /> <br /> I need to start thinking about Legacy now. As mentioned above, there doesn't seem to be any Forces focused Mastigos Legacies, so I could make my own. Any tips on how that could look?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T22:06:39-07:00","id":1382442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382190#post1382190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The symbolism of Hector is its etymological roots, being both a reference to the Trojan warrior Hector denoting heroism, and the later definition of &quot;bully.&quot; He struggles to ride the line of humility and assertiveness in pursuing his goals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Satchel was simply suggesting that the Merit &quot;Shadow Name&quot; would be a worthwhile thing to consider, if you wanted to play up the relevance of the name to your roleplay. It's a pretty nice way to simply have a Yantra in your back pocket, the reliability of which is pretty much fully under your control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T22:18:53-07:00","id":1382445,"title":"","content":"It might be simpler to use one of the pre-existing ones. But anyway, lets take a look at Legacy creation.<br /> <br /> In general, I recommend building the theme first, then figuring out everything else. Mastigos are about <i>Transgression and Confrontation</i> . They understand their vices, confront them, gain mastery over them and thus enlightenment (at least in theory). So your main Arcanum is probably going to be external to the Path (to get a third Ruling), while the optional from it (Space or Mind). Examine how that theme would be aboarded under those lenses, the ones for their Order, their personal philosophy, etc.<br /> <br /> Then you can determine yantras based on flavorful behaviors within that theme. Oblations are habits that further reinforce said mentality.<br /> <br /> For Attainments, a simple way to think about them is:<br /> <br /> 1st: General utility, something simple that you want them to use often.<br /> 2nd: An ability to defend or hide from the main concern of pursuing the theme.<br /> 3rd: The tools needed to operate on the field, whether a way to improvise them or prepare them beforehand. <br /> 4th: Something that demonstrates high mastery of the theme.<br /> 5th: Something that brings them all together.<br /> <br /> For a good format, I recommend the one in the 2ed Legacies thread. The Legacies in my signature also have a design breakdown. It goes through my train of thought for creating them, perhaps it can be of aid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T11:13:48-07:00","id":1382558,"title":"","content":"@Errol216: Thanks for the clarification. I didn\u2019t grasp what Shadow Names are at first read. I don\u2019t have any Merits for it, but maybe I\u2019ll do so later. I might actually make Hector his real name and come up with a Shadow Name later when I get the Merit. Is it expected for a Cabal to know each other\u2019s real names? That would leave them vulnerable to sympathetic magic, right?<br /> <br /> @KaiserAfini: I really like The Agathos Kai Sophos! I\u2019ll work on my own Legacy and your outlines will be very useful. I know it will be Forces based, and if I understand the Attainments correctly I should be able to make some unique spell effects based on standard spells? I ran my Targeted Control Gravity idea by my ST but he says the spell pretty clearly targets an area instead of a subject, so it\u2019s a no go. Could I make that an Attainment instead? This Legacy might turn into the Windrunner Knights Radiant Order. \ud83d\ude0b It could work thematically as well. Every Knight Radiant is in some way a broken person grappling with failure and redemption. Fits a Mastigos pretty well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","user":"ZenBear","date":". 04-19-2020, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T13:11:48-07:00","id":1382581,"title":"","content":"Thank you, glad you liked them. If you want to focus on a more martial side and on concealing weapons, then Space is probably more useful. But if your character is focusing more on the philosophy of transcending the enemy of the Akashayana, then Mind can be a great help.<br /> <br /> Regarding targeted gravitational control, the spell itself at touch range takes the gravity vectors that affect the targets and says &quot;you go that way now&quot;. This is probably how you accomplish a basic gravitational lashing and full adhesion lashing.<br /> <br /> The reverse gravitation lashing is doing the same thing as the <i>Lure &amp; Repel</i> spell from Life, but utilizing Gravity rather than instinct. So its an AoE centered on the intended target. Your spell is reaching out and pulling everything to the focus, like a black hole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T23:40:02-07:00","id":1382686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382558#post1382558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might actually make Hector his real name and come up with a Shadow Name later when I get the Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that you don't need the Merit to have the Shadow Name; you just need it to be able to leverage it in a way that matters to gameplay, i.e. as a Yantra. That's what the XP cost is for.<br /> <br /> Having a Shadow Name is good hygiene for Wisdom, even if you don't lean into it, so you should have one even without the Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382558#post1382558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it expected for a Cabal to know each other\u2019s real names? That would leave them vulnerable to sympathetic magic, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would, because the technical term isn't &quot;real name&quot;; it's &quot;sympathetic name&quot;. Part of the point of a Shadow Name is to play up your &quot;I'm a Mage!&quot; side, but it's also, yes, a great defense mechanism against both Nimbus bleed and people trying to track you or your family down.<br /> <br /> Thus, it's a major sign of trust for the Cabal to share sympathetic names with each other. I'd advise not sharing it by default, simply because it can make for a great bonding moment when you do share it. There are thousands of situations where it could make sense anyways, but as with most defaults, you should have a reason and be deliberate when you mess with it. There was a good AP I read once, for instance, where the cabal's banner-warden had something to prove and gave his sympathetic name to the cabal as part of an aggressive, &quot;I am super-dependable&quot; thing. It's not all that different from handing everyone a loaded gun and then choosing not to wear any defenses around them.<br /> <br /> Also, because sympathetic names don't get a lot of use in most play, it's a good opportunity to have a completely unpronounceable one. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T17:33:04-07:00","id":1382855,"title":"","content":"Heads up for this post, it contains a few more minor spoilers for the Stormlight Archives. If you haven't read it yet, do so!<br /> <br /> I'm working on a couple options for possible Legacies. First option would be to essentially make the Order of Windrunners from Stormlight Archives, but I don't think it will work so well with this character. Still, just for fun I want to explore this idea anyway.<br /> <br /> I would imagine having a Familiar in the form of a Goetia (Honorspren) would be a prerequisite alongside Forces 2, Athletics 2. Initiation into the Legacy would require swearing The First Ideal of the Knights Radiant; &quot;Life before death. Strength before weakness. Journey before destination.&quot; Most First Attainments I see tend to mimic a 1 dot spell, so would a modified version of a 2 dot spell be too much? I would want to grant the Basic Lashing via Targeted Control Gravity. As I mentioned above, my ST won't allow me to do this through typical spellcasting so attaching it to a Legacy is the only way I'll be able to do it. Alternately, the First Attainment could grant a Familiar and I save the Basic Lashing for Second Attainment.<br /> <br /> The Second Ideal is, &quot;I will protect those who cannot protect themselves.&quot; The Second Attainment could be the Basic Lashing as I mentioned above, or it could be Targeted Gravitational Supremacy, essentially granting more control over the Basic Lashing to increase or decrease the effect of gravity as well as determine its direction. This doesn't suit the Ideal as well, but it achieves the mechanics I'm aiming for. I'm not sure what else to put here to match the Ideal. Perhaps it teaches Full Lashing through Gravitational Supremacy increasing the gravity of the target object?<br /> <br /> The Third Ideal is, &quot;I will protect even those I hate, so long as it is right.&quot; For this Third Attainment, I'm not sure what to do but perhaps tie it into Sympathetic Magic? Something like granting bonuses to helping protect people for whom you have a Strong antagonistic Sympathy. Maybe a modification to Turn Momentum to simulate a Reverse Lashing?<br /> <br /> The Fourth Ideal isn't known, but it's theorized to have something to do with accepting that you can't protect everyone. This one seems to lean into Sympathies again. Perhaps it could mimic the &quot;Cut Threads&quot; Space spell?<br /> <br /> The Fifth Ideal hasn't even been hinted at, so I don't know where to go with it. Hopefully more of this will be revealed in the upcoming Rhythm of War book that's projected to release this November! Whatever it turns out to be, I think the Fifth Attainment could have something to do with the Resonance of the Windrunners, which is to say taking on Squires and teaching the Legacy to new Mages.<br /> <br /> This whole concept I feel hearkens back to Mage: Ascension's subjectivity. It would make sense in Ascension for a Mage to invent a Legacy based on a fandom. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ***<br /> <br /> For my second idea, I'm more focused on theme than mechanics. I still want it to be a Forces/Mastigos/Adamantine Arrow Legacy, but beyond that it's up in the air mechanically. I was inspired by Kaiser's Sophos Legacy and its reference to Stoicism, which is a moral philosophy I personally love and adhere to, to an extent. I'm thinking to incorporate Stoicism as the praxis for Confronting one's Jungian Shadow, the embodiment of Transgressive desires.<br /> <br /> For the Attainments, I think Stoicism provides quick and easy First-Fourth Attainment titles with the Four Cardinal Virtues: Wisdom, Courage, Justice, and Temperance. The Fifth Attainment I think should be something like, &quot;No Man Is An Island&quot; to encourage a Stoic of the highest Attainment to spread the Virtues by teaching the Legacy to new Mages.<br /> <br /> There could also be some Attainments revolving around boosting Summoning and resisting demons of Pandemonium to reflect the Legacy's focus on Confronting your Shadow. Optional bonuses with Mind or Space Arcana could specify the Summoning of Wraiths or Imps.<br /> <br /> One way to take advantage of the crossover between Forces, Space, Mind, and Arrow could be to make this a Legacy all about protecting others you are Sympathetically linked to. Allowing you to more easily cast defensive spells at Sympathetic Range for example, or expanding your circle of empathy to more easily make Sympathetic bonds.<br /> <br /> I have fewer ideas for Attainments here, but I like the Stoicism/Shadow combo for a Mastigos Legacy. Tying this theme to Forces and the Adamantine Order would perhaps mean focusing on fighting one's Shadow through direct physical conflict? I really want to find some excuse to tie in TCG, but it would require a lot of Reach <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Maybe it would have to do with the introspective nature of Jungian psychology allowing the Mage to cast area spells on themselves? I don't know.<br /> <br /> Any tips or inspirations for this one would be much appreciated!<br /> <br /> @Errol216: Thanks again! I think I will make Hector Zeroni his sympathetic name and either &quot;Kaladin&quot; or &quot;Kenichi&quot; his Shadow Name, depending on which Legacy I decide to go with. Kaladin is a reference to the Stormlight Archives, Kenichi to a martial arts anime I love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","user":"ZenBear","date":". 04-20-2020, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:27:55-07:00","id":1382878,"title":"","content":"So in summary, the key points so far are:<br /> <br /> 1- They have a moral code<br /> 2- They have an embodied Familiar<br /> 3- They are associated with the simbolism of wind<br /> 4- Gravity and adhesion powers<br /> 5- Its a Mastigos Forces &amp; Mind Legacy<br /> <br /> It might be a good idea to borrow from the paladin's oaths from D&amp;D. I imagine them being some kind of knights errant, sworn to uphold a sacred oath. They embody the ferocity of the dragon (Forces) and the virtue of a knight (Mind). <br /> <br /> The mythological association I can think of are Sigurd and Fafnir, maybe Turin Turambar and Glaurong too. But I think Sir John Lambton might be the closest, since he only slew the Lambton Worm after receiving advice from a wise man.<br /> <br /> Joining the Legacy would require a special Verge, a Supernal Summoning or similar. Sir John would test the candidate to be worthy of upholding the oath of the order and tame the power of the dragon. Success would gain them a Rank 1 embodied familiar sword bound to their Gnosis.<br /> <br /> Every new Attainment would come with a binding clause and a powerful penalty for violating it. They still need to keep the sword fed on Essence and on their side, so its a fine balancing act.<br /> <br /> The main Attainments would concern the Windrunner abilities (first one is the sword, which is powerful enough). If the Attainment's Oaths is challenging enough, it may justify an extra Reach.<br /> <br /> The optional Attainments would focus on the blade. When these mages say their sword's edge cuts through wickedness or its flames only burn the cruel, they mean it literally. Maybe they could only hurt those under a certain Wisdom/Integrity threshold.<br /> <br /> The trick is to find the right blend of the Windrunner's oath with the Adamantine Phalanxes or Stoic virtues.The knights might get a lot of allies from the Black Tower faction of the Arrow (and mentors could have a Ryozanpaku teaching approach)<br /> <br /> Those are the first ideas that come to mind, so they need to be refined. Are they going in the direction of the Windrunners ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T19:44:35-07:00","id":1382881,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar26087_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"26087\" data-vbnamecard=\"26087\">ZenBear</a> congrats! I don\u2019t know enough about M:tAw to offer any suggestions, but I love the Akashayana Mastigos idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T22:55:58-07:00","id":1382908,"title":"","content":"@Kaiser: I love your creativity! You're giving me a ton of inspiration. I'm also glad my references are being understood. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, I'm going to refer back to your list to go down the possible Attainments for the Order of the Windrunners.<br /> <br /> 1st: General utility, something simple that you want them to use often.<br /> I think this is where I grant Lashings, which essentially says all Gravity spells can be cast on a target object or person instead of just on an area.<br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> Optional: Mind 1: Changing direction happens at the speed of thought, requiring no additional actions for casting while any Gravity spell is in effect. This essentially operates like the One Mind, Two Thoughts spell with controlling the spell being one of the extended Mental tasks.<br /> <br /> 2nd: An ability to defend or hide from the main concern of pursuing the theme.<br /> I'm not sure what you mean by this, to be honest. I suppose the &quot;main concern of pursuing the theme&quot; would be facing your Shadow. This could be the Goetia/Honorspren. According to pg. 95 of my pdf, a Mage can only summon a Supernal Entity that corresponds to their Path Ruling Arcana. As such, a Mastigos can only summon Wraiths and Imps, but gaining this Second Attainment grants a Seraphim (Forces) familiar. They are known for giving advice on matters of morality, which would be uniquely helpful to a repentant Mastigos. Starts out as a Rank 1 Supernal Entity.<br /> Prerequisites: Forces 2, Athletics 2, ?<br /> Optional: Mind 2: The Mage and Familiar can communicate telepathically within a certain range.<br /> <br /> 3rd: The tools needed to operate on the field, whether a way to improvise them or prepare them beforehand.<br /> Here is where the Familiar upgrades to Rank 2 and can manifest as a weapon/casting tool. The Familiar can take the form of any weapon desired, and its damage bonus is equal to the Rank of the Goetia (2). If used as a casting tool, it grants the same in bonus dice.<br /> Prerequisites: Forces 3, Athletics 3, Weaponry 3<br /> Optional: Mind 3: Weapon deals psychic damage, ignoring armor, and can damage Twilight entities.<br /> <br /> 4th: Something that demonstrates high mastery of the theme.<br /> So it's again not quite certain until the next book comes out, but it's theorized that once a Windrunner swears to the Fourth Ideal, they get their Shardplate. I don't intend for the Shardblade or Plate to be as OP as in Stormlight, but perhaps a small buff to Forces Mage Armor could approximate the Plate. Maybe you get to add your Familiar's Rank in addition to your Rank in Forces?<br /> Prerequisites: Forces 4, Athletics 4, ?<br /> Optional: Mind 4: Same benefit for Mind Mage Armor.<br /> <br /> 5th: Something that brings them all together.<br /> Still not even a hint of what the Fifth Ideal will be, but I'm pretty committed to the teaching angle so I think I'll use my Resonance idea. Would it be totally out of line to grant a Legacy the ability to safely turn Sleepers into Sleepwalkers? I haven't read up on that section of the book yet. Otherwise maybe he gets free Reach to apply to spell Scale?<br /> Prerequisites: Forces 5, Athletics 5, ?<br /> Optional: Mind 5: ?<br /> <br /> I like the Knight Errant motif! In particular, I would make the Legacy out to be a quest for redemption for past Transgressions. The mythological associations could work as narrative analogues to envisage a devotee's aspirations. Just like in Stormlight, if the Mage Transgresses too blatantly (loses Wisdom) they risk losing the Familiar. Achieving a new rank in the Legacy can restore it. I'm tempted to swap Attainments 1 and 2 as I feel the Familiar is more fundamental than the Lashings and I would prefer to split up the Supernal Entity Rank progression, but I wanted to follow your list. Still contemplating Attainment 5 and the Mind 5 option. I'm not sure, but you had Merits as prerequisites, right? Patient, Eidetic Memory, etc. The ?'s could be Merits to follow suit, but I'm not sure which ones. Maybe Adamant Hand, Astral Adept or Potent Nimbus/Resonance?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","user":"ZenBear","date":". 04-21-2020, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-20T23:35:43-07:00","id":1382913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382908#post1382908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@Kaiser: I love your creativity! You're giving me a ton of inspiration. I'm also glad my references are being understood. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So, I'm going to refer back to your list to go down the possible Attainments for the Order of the Windrunners.<br /> <br /> 1st: General utility, something simple that you want them to use often.<br /> I think this is where I grant Lashings, which essentially says all Gravity spells can be cast on a target object or person instead of just on an area.<br /> Prerequisites: Initiation<br /> Optional: Mind 1: Changing direction happens at the speed of thought, requiring no additional actions for casting while any Gravity spell is in effect. This essentially operates like the One Mind, Two Thoughts spell with controlling the spell being one of the extended Mental tasks.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Lashings are at least Forces 2 and cannot really be a first attainment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2nd: An ability to defend or hide from the main concern of pursuing the theme.<br /> I'm not sure what you mean by this, to be honest. I suppose the &quot;main concern of pursuing the theme&quot; would be facing your Shadow. This could be the Goetia/Honorspren. According to pg. 95 of my pdf, a Mage can only summon a Supernal Entity that corresponds to their Path Ruling Arcana. As such, a Mastigos can only summon Wraiths and Imps, but gaining this Second Attainment grants a Seraphim (Forces) familiar. They are known for giving advice on matters of morality, which would be uniquely helpful to a repentant Mastigos. Starts out as a Rank 1 Supernal Entity. </div> </div> </div>Supernal Entities cannot be familiars. Goetia are not Supernal Entities (they are Astral). &quot;Seraphim&quot; is plural, &quot;seraph&quot; is the singular.<br /> Further, adding a ruling Arcanum does not expand the list of tyoes of Supernal entities you can summon, that is solely a product of your Path and does not change from picking up a Legacy.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prerequisites: Forces 2, Athletics 2, ?<br /> Optional: Mind 2: The Mage and Familiar can communicate telepathically within a certain range. </div> </div> </div>Granting the Familiar manifestation is a Spirit/Death/Mind 4 spell (based on type of familiar). You could make joining the legacy require the Mage to already have a familiar of the appropriate type or make part of the initiation receiving one granted by a mentor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3rd: The tools needed to operate on the field, whether a way to improvise them or prepare them beforehand.<br /> Here is where the Familiar upgrades to Rank 2 and can manifest as a weapon/casting tool. The Familiar can take the form of any weapon desired, and its damage bonus is equal to the Rank of the Goetia (2). If used as a casting tool, it grants the same in bonus dice. </div> </div> </div>Forces has nothing to do with Goetia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Prerequisites: Forces 3, Athletics 3, Weaponry 3<br /> Optional: Mind 3: Weapon deals psychic damage, ignoring armor, and can damage Twilight entities. </div> </div> </div>Causing a weapon (Matter) to deal psychic damage (Mind) would require both Mind and Matter.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4th: Something that demonstrates high mastery of the theme.<br /> So it's again not quite certain until the next book comes out, but it's theorized that once a Windrunner swears to the Fourth Ideal, they get their Shardplate. I don't intend for the Shardblade or Plate to be as OP as in Stormlight, but perhaps a small buff to Forces Mage Armor could approximate the Plate. Maybe you get to add your Familiar's Rank in addition to your Rank in Forces?<br /> Prerequisites: Forces 4, Athletics 4, ?<br /> Optional: Mind 4: Same benefit for Mind Mage Armor. </div> </div> </div>A Familiar's rank caps at 2, so this isn't an amazing benefit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5th: Something that brings them all together.<br /> Still not even a hint of what the Fifth Ideal will be, but I'm pretty committed to the teaching angle so I think I'll use my Resonance idea. Would it be totally out of line to grant a Legacy the ability to safely turn Sleepers into Sleepwalkers? </div> </div> </div>Yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't read up on that section of the book yet. Otherwise maybe he gets free Reach to apply to spell Scale?<br /> Prerequisites: Forces 5, Athletics 5, ?<br /> Optional: Mind 5: ? </div> </div> </div>True flight, greater gravity manipulation, or something along those lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like the Knight Errant motif! In particular, I would make the Legacy out to be a quest for redemption for past Transgressions. The mythological associations could work as narrative analogues to envisage a devotee's aspirations. Just like in Stormlight, if the Mage Transgresses too blatantly (loses Wisdom) they risk losing the Familiar. Achieving a new rank in the Legacy can restore it. I'm tempted to swap Attainments 1 and 2 as I feel the Familiar is more fundamental than the Lashings and I would prefer to split up the Supernal Entity Rank progression, but I wanted to follow your list. Still contemplating Attainment 5 and the Mind 5 option. I'm not sure, but you had Merits as prerequisites, right? Patient, Eidetic Memory, etc. The ?'s could be Merits to follow suit, but I'm not sure which ones. Maybe Adamant Hand, Astral Adept or Potent Nimbus/Resonance? </div> </div> </div><br /> Personally, I don't think the Windrunners really fit the Mastigos very well, thematically; they feel more Obrimos or Acanthus. The fatebinders seem more Mastigos-y","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":2757,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","user":"proindrakenzol","date":". 04-21-2020, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T02:44:45-07:00","id":1382935,"title":"","content":"@proindrakerzol damn you\u2019re picky...<br /> <br /> People should be allowed to build their characters the way they want without worrying about so many details.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T02:48:22-07:00","id":1382936,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2757_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2757\" data-vbnamecard=\"2757\">proindrakenzol</a> and your name is hard to spell \ud83d\ude02, but that\u2019s not your fault. People get mine wrong too (my real name and my screen name).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T02:57:14-07:00","id":1382937,"title":"","content":"On second thought, I take it back. The OP was specifically asking for rules advice and you gave it to him. My bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T12:35:41-07:00","id":1383015,"title":"","content":"Having a Supernal entity familiar should probably be impossible. I was imagining that the trial would involve inhering the seat or being chosen by a spirit of the Legacy. Since goetia can't Manifest, this opened up the possibility of a spirit or ghost of a former knight being called forth by an ancient covenant with the entity. Perhaps they already need a specific kind of familiar to undertake the with them or the goetia gains the ability to Materialize as a sword via the initiation. It all depends on what direction you want to go with their lore. Maybe they only receive it as part of the higher Attainments.<br /> <br /> The Attainments need to be compatible with their level of the Arcanum. With that in mind, here are some general ideas:<br /> <br /> Forces 1: Nightvision with Reach assigned to instant use. A simple skill that helps them fight and perceive the world around them in more detail by seeing through the dragon's eyes.<br /> <br /> Mind 1: A knight must be careful of who they serve and protect. He must also know how to establish a rapport with his allies. To this end, the first thing they learn is how to understand people. This acts as Know Nature with Reach assigned to instant use.<br /> <br /> Forces 2: Kinetic Efficiency with Reach assigned to instant use and advanced duration. This represents their ability to duck, weave, climb and jump to adapt to the battlefield. <br /> <br /> Mind 2: Emotional Urging with Reach assigned to instant use and sensory range. To compensate for the extra Reach, it can only be used when they are disarmed. This covers a knight's ability to be inspiring to his allies and terrifying to his enemies.<br /> <br /> Forces 3: Gravity Control with Reach used for instant use and advanced scale. It can be used as touch or as an aimed spell. So it covers both Lashings at once, as the dragon roars or draws breath.<br /> <br /> Mind 3: After summoning Sir Lambton and passing his trial, you receive a Rank 2 goetia familiar with the ability to Manifest as a simple weapon. When creating the familiar, the Blast Numina can be used for sword beams or as a replacement for ammo. <br /> <br /> Forces 4: Spend a scene and a mana to ritually dedicate a weapon to your cause, allowing it to deal aggravated damage (not 100% sure if this is possible). It represents wielding the dragon's fire.<br /> <br /> Mind 4: The goetia gains a variation of the Stalwart Numina that grants its Power as base armor for a target. This manifests as an energy armor (like Dragonborn's Dragon Aspect).<br /> <br /> Mind typically has no way to make someone a Sleepwalker, that is normally the purview of Prime or Fate. I use it as the fourth optional Attainment of the Szary Stra\u017cnik Legacy, which utilizes both. <br /> <br /> I try to design the capstone to elevate the utility of all the Attainments.<br /> <br /> The Sophos need time to make plans. Without it they have no benefits from hung spells, no rewrite histories, no rote action, nothing. Furthermore, plans need to coordinate multiple individuals. So their capstone lets them always have an army of loyal, well coordinated, peak human skill supernatural specialists. Not only that, the optional one gives them the time to plan. Together they equip them to implement their philosophy in any situation.<br /> <br /> Now they can make a temporal bubble, astrally project to scout and setup goetia. Then Veil of Moments gives them the comfort to heal and scour for mana. Then they can setup everything before time resumes. So in a turn, the invaders who kicked in the door of the cabal's Sanctum go from having the edge to being routed. <br /> <br /> The Stra\u017cnik get a reinforcement to their theme of indirect manipulators, ghosts in the system. The main Attainment gives a lot of flexibility to control the board, shifting Obsessions and merits as needed. The secondary one lets them prepare care packages and is a discrete method of manipulation that maintains plausible deniability. In short, they synergize with the other Attainments.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, here are my current ideas:<br /> <br /> Forces 5: Levitation with Reach assigned to advanced duration and free flight. This represents the idea of a dragon taking flight.<br /> <br /> Mind 5: Psychic Reprogramming with Reach assigned to instant use and advanced duration. It ends if the target suffers any Breaking Point and they invariably know its the caster's fault. After all, knights need to adhere to a higher standard than causing suffering to those they &quot;conscript&quot;.<br /> <br /> This should allow them to sneak in to convince or recruit the opposition. Alternatively, they can use it to rain death upon their enemies.<br /> <br /> Added to the Space Arcanum, it gives them a lot of freedom both in and out of combat. The biggest problem is that I accidentally made Talion and Calebrimbor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 04-21-2020, 04:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T13:27:48-07:00","id":1383025,"title":"","content":"Supernal Familiar isn't exactly a thing, but you can tinker around with some other stuff to get close. Supernal Watcher, Mystery Commands, blade and plate being Boons or something else that you gain access to via some specialized interaction with a Supernal Entity, etc.<br /> <br /> Edit: Imo, the Windrunners would be Forces and Prime, delving deep into the Obrimos views on structure and heirarchy since they're called out as one of the most regimented Orders and their founders took after Jezrien the king of kings. You can see how it plays out with Kaladin too, always somehow ending up in a position of authority.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 04-21-2020, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T13:32:28-07:00","id":1383027,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24280_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24280\" data-vbnamecard=\"24280\">KaiserAfini</a> I'd swap Kinetic Efficiency and Nightvision. KE just needs Advanced Duration, instant casting gives you nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T13:40:33-07:00","id":1383029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1383027#post1383027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> I'd swap Kinetic Efficiency and Nightvision. KE just needs Advanced Duration, instant casting gives you nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, good call.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T14:55:02-07:00","id":1383039,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382913#post1382913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lashings are at least Forces 2 and cannot really be a first attainment.</div> </div> </div> </div>So all Attainments should correspond with a spell of equal dots? If they correspond with a spell at all that is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382913#post1382913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernal Entities cannot be familiars. Goetia are not Supernal Entities (they are Astral). &quot;Seraphim&quot; is plural, &quot;seraph&quot; is the singular.<br /> Further, adding a ruling Arcanum does not expand the list of tyoes of Supernal entities you can summon, that is solely a product of your Path and does not change from picking up a Legacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is me conflating terms again, my bad. I think Goetia fit the Spren perfectly. Both are embodiments of concepts, sort of like Platonic Ideals. A Goetia of Honor would work out as an Honorspren. I didn't mean to suggest that a Windrunner would be able to summon Seraphim like they do Wraiths and Imps, just that by devoting to the Legacy they get a Seraph Goetia. I now understand why that doesn't make sense. Still, the idea of a Mastigos seeking guidance from an Angel of the Aether is compelling.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382913#post1382913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Granting the Familiar manifestation is a Spirit/Death/Mind 4 spell (based on type of familiar). You could make joining the legacy require the Mage to already have a familiar of the appropriate type or make part of the initiation receiving one granted by a mentor.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that makes a certain sense. Either through the spell of a higher Mastigos member of the Legacy or perhaps through direct appeal to the Aether in a Supernal Verge, the adherent gains a Familiar. Would this be too much for a First Attainment?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382913#post1382913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces has nothing to do with Goetia.</div> </div> </div> </div>So being that Forces is the focus of the Legacy, all Attainments must be based in Forces? Makes sense, I just thought I could be a bit more flexible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382913#post1382913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Causing a weapon (Matter) to deal psychic damage (Mind) would require both Mind and Matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, though in this case it's not really a weapon (Matter) but rather a manifesting Goetia, which I would see as a Mind effect. To quote the pdf: &quot;Goetia cannot naturally Manifest, and must be granted the ability to do so through magic.&quot; I figured an Attainment could grant such ability without needing Matter Arcana specifically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382913#post1382913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Familiar's rank caps at 2, so this isn't an amazing benefit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to be conservative. Would doubling your Forces Rank be too much?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>proindrakenzol</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1382913#post1382913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I don't think the Windrunners really fit the Mastigos very well, thematically; they feel more Obrimos or Acanthus. The fatebinders seem more Mastigos-y</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree 100%, I was just trying to fit a square peg in a round hole so I could play the Legacy with my Mastigos character. I'll keep tinkering with the Windrunner Legacy in a separate thread but it will be Obrimos. Who are the fatebinders, by the way? That's not one of the Knights Radiant Orders. I think Mastigos would best fit the Elsecallers, what with Space Arcana, though Soulcasting seems like a Matter power. Surgebinding and Arcanum don't match 1 to 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26087,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","user":"ZenBear","date":". 04-21-2020, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26087-zenbear","name":"ZenBear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26087_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T15:15:51-07:00","id":1383040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZenBear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1383039#post1383039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So all Attainments should correspond with a spell of equal dots? If they correspond with a spell at all that is.</div> </div> </div> </div>All spell-based Attainments should be a spell of equal or lower dots. The reason you would use a lower level spell is to give it more reach effects.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is me conflating terms again, my bad. I think Goetia fit the Spren perfectly. Both are embodiments of concepts, sort of like Platonic Ideals. A Goetia of Honor would work out as an Honorspren. I didn't mean to suggest that a Windrunner would be able to summon Seraphim like they do Wraiths and Imps, just that by devoting to the Legacy they get a Seraph Goetia. I now understand why that doesn't make sense. Still, the idea of a Mastigos seeking guidance from an Angel of the Aether is compelling. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I think the Spren are more like Spirits. Goetia conform to and change with human ideals, whereas spirits are much less human-centric, but that's not really important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that makes a certain sense. Either through the spell of a higher Mastigos member of the Legacy or perhaps through direct appeal to the Aether in a Supernal Verge, the adherent gains a Familiar. Would this be too much for a First Attainment? </div> </div> </div>The Aether is inaccessible to Mastigos and Goetia come from the Astral, anyway. I would just make having the Familiar merit with an Honor goetia be a prerequisite for the Legacy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So being that Forces is the focus of the Legacy, all Attainments must be based in Forces? Makes sense, I just thought I could be a bit more flexible. </div> </div> </div>All the primary attainments must be Forces based in some way, yes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fair enough, though in this case it's not really a weapon (Matter) but rather a manifesting Goetia, which I would see as a Mind effect. To quote the pdf: &quot;Goetia cannot naturally Manifest, and must be granted the ability to do so through magic.&quot; I figured an Attainment could grant such ability without needing Matter Arcana specifically.<br /> <br /> <br /> I was trying to be conservative. Would doubling your Forces Rank be too much? </div> </div> </div>Making a Goetia take the form of an energy blade would be a Forces 4/Mind 4 effect and could work as the Mind 4 alternate Attainment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I agree 100%, I was just trying to fit a square peg in a round hole so I could play the Legacy with my Mastigos character. I'll keep tinkering with the Windrunner Legacy in a separate thread but it will be Obrimos. Who are the fatebinders, by the way? That's not one of the Knights Radiant Orders. I think Mastigos would best fit the Elsecallers, what with Space Arcana, though Soulcasting seems like a Matter power. Surgebinding and Arcanum don't match 1 to 1. </div> </div> </div>For some reason I thought the Skybreakers were fatebinders, I honestly have no idea why.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T16:11:52-07:00","id":1383051,"title":"","content":"You might have been thinking of the Bond Smiths.<br /> <br /> I tend to think of the Spren as Supernal Beings. Spren and some of the stuff they're connected to cross too many conceptual boundaries. Like, you need a spren to act as the translator to the spren of others things to affect them with Soul Casting, they have almost no way of physically interacting with the world except via turning into a blade and maybe plate, the bond is what surgebinders derive their power from much like Mages drawing on the Supernal in the first place, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T16:37:14-07:00","id":1383053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1383051#post1383051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might have been thinking of the Bond Smiths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe? They'd make an interesting Fate/Space or Matter/Space Legacy, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I tend to think of the Spren as Supernal Beings. Spren and some of the stuff they're connected to cross too many conceptual boundaries. Like, you need a spren to act as the translator to the spren of others things to affect them with Soul Casting, they have almost no way of physically interacting with the world except via turning into a blade and maybe plate, the bond is what surgebinders derive their power from much like Mages drawing on the Supernal in the first place, etc. </div> </div> </div>See, to me that describes spirits. Some spirits live in twilight in the physical world, but most live in a difficult to access (but still physically accessible place); every object and emotion has a spirit associated with it; and spirits feed on the existence of the thing they represent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-21T18:53:57-07:00","id":1383064,"title":"","content":"Yeah, spirits are a pretty close equivalent. They're not quite...I dunno, removed enough? For me to consider them the natural fit, or maybe I just want something special because any Mage can have a Familiar Bond. There's also a question of how willing a spirit would be to allow itself to be changed as happens with Soulcasting, like from a a chalice to a bunch of blood is essentially to die in some sense. Spirits as Spren is a pretty good fit though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T13:59:11-07:00","id":1384257,"title":"","content":"So, this legacy he's going for has Forces and Space as fundamentals.<br /> <br /> Why not tweak the rationale of Ground Eater a whit so it's a gravity-based woojie whammy? Alter the special effects so a victim is heavier on their feet and fighting unpredictable gravity. An aided person is lighter on their feet with surer stride. Include fancy options like running up walls with the enhanced movement for the Duration or if the movement can be dropped to zero, the target collapses as if tripped or they cannot move at all or something.<br /> <br /> This might <i>still </i>be better as the second dot so it can use Advanced Duration, but it could represent an Influence Gravity option that works with Space to isolate the target rather than targeting an area. Solves game balance issues pretty well and fits what I <i>think</i> is the desired result.<br /> <br /> Certainly once you hit attainment 4 or 5, you could use Alter Direction as the attainment, Forces focus notwithstanding, to allow free manipulation of gravity or momentum. These things might need some adjustment to keep the optimal flavor, but Space and Forces are the proper arcana to govern that sort of thing. <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't recognize the source material, so I'm not diving all in on this one.<br /> <br /> The idea of finding a wiser source to help direct confrontation and challenge to things that actually matter would not be a <i>normal</i> Mastigos approach, but it certainly could be one. I bet there's a twist that makes them fit Mastigos just peachy, though that might shift emphasis away from desired points.<br /> <br /> One possibility that leaped to mind: The tutor is the Mastigos' own Daimon, so they are actually sizing their own mind and whipping it into shape. (Perhaps with the aid of their tutor or some angelic force) Joining the legacy helps purify that vision and requires an ordeal to establish the Daimon as a force for good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T15:49:51-07:00","id":1384284,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1384257#post1384257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recognize the source material, so I'm not diving all in on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this doesn't come off as dismissive, but I'd recommend reading the Stormlight Archive then in order to know what the discussion is about instead of throwing in suggestions that...don't really fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T15:49:51-07:00","id":1384285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1384257#post1384257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't recognize the source material, so I'm not diving all in on this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope this doesn't come off as dismissive, but I'd recommend reading the Stormlight Archive then in order to know what the discussion is about instead of throwing in suggestions that...don't really fit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:40:16-07:00","id":1384322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1381110-first-mage?p=1384257#post1384257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, this legacy he's going for has Forces and Space as fundamentals.<br /> <br /> Why not tweak the rationale of Ground Eater a whit so it's a gravity-based woojie whammy? Alter the special effects so a victim is heavier on their feet and fighting unpredictable gravity. An aided person is lighter on their feet with surer stride. Include fancy options like running up walls with the enhanced movement for the Duration or if the movement can be dropped to zero, the target collapses as if tripped or they cannot move at all or something.<br /> <br /> This might <i>still </i>be better as the second dot so it can use Advanced Duration, but it could represent an Influence Gravity option that works with Space to isolate the target rather than targeting an area. Solves game balance issues pretty well and fits what I <i>think</i> is the desired result.<br /> <br /> Certainly once you hit attainment 4 or 5, you could use Alter Direction as the attainment, Forces focus notwithstanding, to allow free manipulation of gravity or momentum. These things might need some adjustment to keep the optimal flavor, but Space and Forces are the proper arcana to govern that sort of thing. <br /> <br /> <br /> I don't recognize the source material, so I'm not diving all in on this one.<br /> <br /> The idea of finding a wiser source to help direct confrontation and challenge to things that actually matter would not be a <i>normal</i> Mastigos approach, but it certainly could be one. I bet there's a twist that makes them fit Mastigos just peachy, though that might shift emphasis away from desired points.<br /> <br /> One possibility that leaped to mind: The tutor is the Mastigos' own Daimon, so they are actually sizing their own mind and whipping it into shape. (Perhaps with the aid of their tutor or some angelic force) Joining the legacy helps purify that vision and requires an ordeal to establish the Daimon as a force for good.</div> </div> </div> </div>For a quick reference of the powers, I recommend these articles.<br /> <br /> The Knights themselves: <br /> <a href=\"https://coppermind.net/wiki/Order_of_Windrunners\" target=\"_blank\">https://coppermind.net/wiki/Order_of_Windrunners</a><br /> <br /> Their living blades:<br /> <a href=\"https://coppermind.net/wiki/Shardblade\" target=\"_blank\">https://coppermind.net/wiki/Shardblade</a><br /> <br /> Their armor:<br /> <a href=\"https://coppermind.net/wiki/Shardplate\" target=\"_blank\">https://coppermind.net/wiki/Shardplate</a><br /> <br /> They sound like specialized Manifestations of ephemeral entities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}